":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114671","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114671","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114671.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114671.patch","merged_at":"2026-04-09T22:48:09Z"},"body":"This PR adds new export options to customize the Android native splash screen.\r\nCurrently, customization is already possible via [custom theme attributes](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_editorexportplatformandroid.html#class-editorexportplatformandroid-property-gradle-build-custom-theme-attributes) but it's only for Gradle builds, and requires manually placing the files in the `drawable` folder.\r\n\r\nWith this PR:\r\n- Users can now easily set a custom splash screen icon, background color, and branding image.\r\n- It is now also supported for legacy export builds.\r\n- Added an option to disable Godot's boot splash.\r\n    - On Android, Godot apps currently display two splash screens: first the Android system splash, followed by the Godot boot splash. With this new export option, the Android native splash is shown for longer, until engine finishes loading.\r\n\r\ncloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/13360","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}